First, use the distributive property to factor. $\begin{align*}
664\times494&=(664\times500)+664\times(-6)\\
&=(664\times500)+(664\times(100-6))\\
&=(664\times500)+664(100-6)\text{ now let }2x=500\text{and }3y=600-6.\\
&=\boxed{664(2x+3y)}
\end{align*}$ Factor 2x+3y. $2x+3y=2(500)+3(600-6)$ Add 2x+3y and $\boxed{574280}$ The final answer is \textbf{574280}.

1. Express 109 as \(100 + 9\).
   Thus, \(109 = 100 + 9\).

2. Expand the product:
   \begin{align*}
   305 \times 109 &= 305 \times (100 + 9) \\
   &= 305 \times 100 + 305 \times 9 \quad \text{(multiplying by the number of times 100 goes into 109)}\\
   &= 30500 + 2745 \quad \text{(multiplying 305 and 9)}
   \end{align*}
3. The sum of \(30500\) and \(2745\) is \(33245\).
   Thus, \(305 \times 109 = 33245\).
